          "english": "While this research into gratitude is relatively new, the principles involved are anything but. Students of mine in a political philosophy course at Indiana University are reading Daniel Defoe's 300-year-old Robinson Crusoe, often regarded as the first novel published in English. Left alone on an unknown island with no apparent prospect of rescue or escape, Crusoe has much to lament(悲叹). But instead of giving in to despair, he makes a list of things for which he is grateful, including the fact that he is the sole survivor from the shipwreck(海难) and has been able to salvage many useful items from the wreckage.",
          "chinese": "虽然对感恩的这类研究相对较新，但其中涉及的原则却绝非新鲜。我的一些印第安纳大学政治哲学课学生正在阅读丹尼尔·笛福三百年前创作的《鲁滨逊漂流记》，这部作品通常被认为是用英语出版的第一部小说。鲁滨逊独自一人被困在一座陌生岛屿上，显然没有获救或逃脱的希望，有许多事情值得悲叹。但他没有陷入绝望，而是列出了一些值得感恩的事情，其中包括自己是这场海难中唯一的幸存者，并且能够从残骸中抢救出许多有用的物品。",
