          "number": 11,
          "letter": "K",
          "english": "Reflecting on generosity and gratitude, the great basketball coach John Wooden once offered two counsels to his players and students. First, he said, \"It is impossible to have a perfect day unless you have done something for someone who will never be able to repay you.\" In saying this, Wooden sought to promote purely generous acts, as opposed to those performed with an expectation of reward. Second, he said, \"Give thanks for your blessings every day.\"",
